Modifications
-------------
The decoder parses untrusted files. Apple's reference leaves packet- and
cookie-declared sizes unchecked, so a crafted stream can read or write past the
decoder's buffers or execute an undefined shift. Orca adds bounds and value
checks in the file's own RequireAction style. Every valid stream decodes to the
same samples. Each modified file carries "Modified by Orca; see ORCA-CHANGES."
after Apple's licence header. Line numbers below are the upstream originals.

ALACDecoder.cpp
  Init (frma/alac atom skips, :102, :109): require >= 12 cookie bytes remain
    before reading cookie[4..7] and subtracting 12, so a short cookie cannot
    over-read or underflow theCookieBytesRemaining.
  Decode, SCE/LFE and CPE:
    - after computing chanBits: require 1 <= chanBits <= 32, so the dynamic
      predictor and bit reader never shift by 0 or >= 32.
    - after a partial-frame numSamples read: require 1 <= numSamples <=
      frameLength, so a frame cannot claim more samples than the buffers hold.
    - after the last coefficient table read: require cur <= end.
    - after advancing past the shift-off region: require cur <= end.
    - before an uncompressed (escape) frame's sample reads: require the frame's
      sample bits (numSamples*chanBits, doubled for a pair) fit the bytes left.
  Decode, CPE only: after reading mixBits, require mixBits <= 31 (unmix shifts
    right by mixBits).
  Decode, ID_END: after the closing byte-align, require cur <= end.
  Decode: the "decoded all channels" break was compiled only when !DEBUG; make
    it unconditional so a bitstream with extra elements cannot run on.
  Decode, NoMoreChannels: add the missing bit-depth 20 case so unfilled 20-bit
    channels are zeroed like 16/24/32.

ag_dec.c
  dyn_decomp (:290): measure maxPos from the current read position (end - cur)
    rather than the whole packet (byteSize), so the "ran off the end" check
    stops the Golomb reader at the real packet end.
  dyn_decomp (:337): require the zero-run Golomb parameter k <= 31 before it is
    used as a right-shift amount in dyn_get, so a crafted packet that drives the
    mean estimator's wrap arithmetic cannot shift by 32 or more (undefined, and
    a sanitizer abort in release builds). A valid stream keeps k in 1..9.

dp_dec.c
  unpc_block (:64): compute denhalf as 0 when denshift is 0 instead of shifting
    by -1 (undefined). denhalf is the round-to-nearest addend applied before the
    predictor's right shift of denshift, so 0 is the correct addend when no
    shift is applied; the value is unchanged for denshift >= 1.
  unpc_block (:97): clamp the warm-up loop to j < num so a frame shorter than
    the predictor order cannot write past the output buffer; unchanged when
    num > numactive, which holds for every full frame.

Shim (liborca/codec/alac_shim.cpp)
  Reads a few bytes past the packet end remain in the reference bit reader
  (ALACBitUtilities.c, ag_dec.c); the shim copies each packet into a buffer
  padded and zero-filled past its end so those reads stay in allocated memory.
  It also validates the ALACSpecificConfig before Init (frameLength 1..65536,
  bitDepth in {16,20,24,32}, numChannels 1..kALACMaxChannels, kb 1..31,
  compatibleVersion 0), so no oversized cookie reaches Init and the Golomb
  reader's shifts by kb and 32-k stay defined (kb 0 would shift by 32).
